    feat(auth): log structured WARN on every HTTP 429 rate-limit refusal
    
    The token-bucket limiter silently swallowed refusals — no operator
    signal when an IP was being throttled. Every 429 now emits one
    console.warn JSON line (level, event=rate_limit_refused, ip, limit,
    remaining=0, retryAfter) with the same retryAfter value the client
    receives in Retry-After. Observability fields only: no auth headers,
    request bodies, or secrets. Response body and headers unchanged.
    
    Prior worker left tests-only in the tree; this commit pairs them with
    the source change.
    
    Addresses RATE-LIMIT-001
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
